<article class="env-lemma" id="0DRN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DRN">Lemma <span data-tag="0DRN">107.5.9</span>.</a> Suppose given a Cartesian square of morphisms of locally Noetherian stacks </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{T}' \ar[d]\ar[r] &  \mathcal{T} \ar[d] \\  \mathcal{X}' \ar[r] &  \mathcal{X} }  \]
</div>
  <p> in which the vertical morphisms are locally of finite type. If $t' \in |\mathcal{T}'|$, with images $t$, $x'$, and $x$ in $|\mathcal{T}|$, $|\mathcal{X}'|$, and $|\mathcal{X}|$ respectively, then $\dim _{t'}(\mathcal{T}'_{x'}) = \dim _{t}(\mathcal{T}_ x).$ </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Both sides can (by definition) be computed as the dimension of the same fibre product. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>